  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (HEST4-6/PL00, HEST4-5/PL01, HEST4-5/PL03, HEST4-5/PL04, HEST4-5/PL05, HEST4-5/PL06, HEST4-5/PL10, HEST4-5/PL13 and Design and Access Statement. Received: 19th March 2013. HEST4-5/PL02A. Received; 16th May 2013 ) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - The 38 parking spaces as indicated on plan HEST4-5/PL02A shall be permanently retained for use by Unit 4 and 5, Heston Centre, International Avenue, Hounslow and shall not be used for any other purposes or by any other unit, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 4 - Before the use hereby approved commences details shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority for the design, size and location of the proposed cycle store. \r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - No fans, louvres, ducts or other external plant shall be installed without the prior approval of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - Prior to occupation of the site a Strategic Level Travel plan shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The travel plan should cover all uses in the wider industrial estate controlled by the applicant. Further information on travel planning can be found at http://www.lscp.org.uk/newwaytoplan/resources. \r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 7 - Before the use hereby approved commences the vehicular crossover and gates as approved by application 01499/C24/P3 on the 9th October 2012 shall be implemented in strict accordance with the approved plans unless otherwise agreed in writing with the Local Planning Authority."
  ],
